research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.log-4286-research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.provenance.jsonl-35-{"id":"cex-comparison-needs-nonnegativity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"The item is the standard direct-comparison theorem with its nonnegativity hypothesis removed, refuted by the negative harmonic series below the zero series. That is a recoverable alteration of the sourced theorem, not a novel mathematical claim. The explicit signed witness and verification are locally chosen.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.log-4287-research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.provenance.jsonl-36-{"id":"cex-condensation-needs-monotonicity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.rice.edu/~semmes/math331.pdf"],"rationale":"The item is Cauchy condensation with the sourced monotonicity hypothesis deleted. Its power-of-two zero set is a concrete local witness: the condensed series vanishes while the original terms equal 1 arbitrarily late. The false proposition is a recoverable alteration; the witness proof is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.log-4288-research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.provenance.jsonl-37-{"id":"cex-limit-comparison-l-zero-one-directional","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://sites.und.edu/timothy.prescott/apex/web/apex.Ch9.S4.html","https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"The UND statement gives only the direction from convergence of the larger comparison series to convergence of the smaller series when the quotient limit is zero. The item reverses that sourced implication and refutes it with the standard p=2 versus p=1 pair. The indexed verification is locally written.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
