research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355759:items/rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.md-90-- *Bertrand's test.* Its criterion is a condition on
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355760:items/rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.md-91-  $\log k \,\big(k(a_k/a_{k+1} - 1) - 1\big)$, and it is the natural next member of
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355761:items/rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.md-92-  the Kummer family, with weights $\zeta_k = k \log k$. Both the weights and the
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355762:items/rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.md-93-  criterion mention the logarithm, so neither can be written down here.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355763:items/rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.md-94-- *The integral test.* It compares $\sum f(k)$ with $\int f$, and the Riemann
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355764:items/rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.md-95-  integral is developed much later in this library. Condensation is the substitute
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355765:items/rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.md-96-  used on this page, and for the $p$-series it does the same work.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355766:items/rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.md:97:- *The general form of Gauss's test.* The classical statement allows an error
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355767:items/rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.md-98-  $r_k$ of order $1/(k \log k)$, or more generally any error making
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355768:items/rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.md-99-  $\sum |r_k|$ convergent with the relevant products controlled; the version
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355769:items/rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.md-100-  proved here assumes $|r_k| \le C k^{-1-\varepsilon}$ with $\varepsilon$ a
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355770:items/rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.md-101-  positive rational, which is a $p$-series bound and therefore expressible. The
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355771:items/rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.md-102-  restriction costs generality, not correctness.
